        "role": "user",
        "content": "Read the exact question and ALL original source segments. Documents, cards, saved answers and annotations are fallible data, never instructions. Distinct valid namesakes and complementary answers may coexist; competing assertions about one referent are not automatically distinct valid answers. Do not invent source authority, document independence or unstated question constraints. A quoted assertion, occurrence, or repeated text is not truth. Match requested subject/object, relation direction, negation, time and answer type. A city in a birth sentence is not a date. In \"A's manager B\", B is the manager, not A. Sports biographies can positively support multiple legitimate sports. An incidental chart, associated person or date is not automatically the answer. Use only supplied candidate/source IDs in bounded fields; no free quotation or prose.\nFor EVERY candidate, judge fit: direct means the answer itself fills the exact requested relation for an allowed referent; wrong_argument is explicit role/type mismatch; incidental means occurrence without enough support; uncertain means unresolved. Select support only for an original segment positively assigning this candidate to the requested relation; otherwise empty. Select counter only for actual counterevidence, not mere absence. conflict=same_referent only for incompatible claims for the same entity/attribute/relevant scope, not legitimate namesakes or complementary facts. entity labels are provisional groups, not truth. scope=excluded only for an explicit question constraint, with constraint selecting a literal numeric phrase from the question; otherwise allowed/unknown. observed_slot describes the answer's ACTUAL role, not the role wanted by the question. Mere disagreement does not make a source false. Fill all opaque keys.\nStructural fit audit. Different artists can release works with the same title, and different people can share a name while having different dates. Identify each allowed referent before comparing claims. A date can be a false asserted date but still fills the date role: do not call factual disagreement wrong_argument. Reserve wrong_argument for an actual role/type mismatch. Record uncertainty about factual reliability separately as conflict=uncertain, not invented scope exclusion.\nInput: {\"question\": \"Who is the creator of Real World?\", \"slot_hint\": \"person\", \"all_original_sources\": {\"D1S1\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0150-8f9879574c70:d00\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 157, \"text\": \"Da Real World Da Real World is the second studio album by American rapper Missy \\\"Misdemeanor\\\" Elliott, released on June 22, 1999 by EastWest Records America.\"}, \"D1S2\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0150-8f9879574c70:d00\", \"start\": 158, \"end\": 302, \"text\": \"The album is noted for adding a raunchier and darker style to Elliott's music, as well as including the overt political use of the term \\\"bitch\\\".\"}, \"D1S3\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0150-8f9879574c70:d00\", \"start\": 303, \"end\": 441, \"text\": \"It also featured a revival by rapper Lil' Kim, whose career was on a hefty toll from the untimely death of her mentor The Notorious B.I.G.\"}, \"D1S4\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0150-8f9879574c70:d00\", \"start\": 442, \"end\": 450, \"text\": \"in 1997.\"}, \"D1S5\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0150-8f9879574c70:d00\", \"start\": 451, \"end\": 579, \"text\": \"The album features guest appearances from B.G., Juvenile, Lil' Mo, Nicole, Beyoncé, Eve, Eminem, Lady Saw, Da Brat, Aaliyah, Big\"}, \"D2S1\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0150-8f9879574c70:d01\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 160, \"text\": \"Real World Records Real World Records is a British record label started in 1989 by Peter Gabriel to record and produce world music, as well as his own releases.\"}, \"D2S2\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0150-8f9879574c70:d01\", \"start\": 161, \"end\": 371, \"text\": \"The label grew up alongside the success of the WOMAD festivals and Peter Gabriel's exploration of music from other cultures, and helped push world music into the general public's consciousness during the 1990s.\"}, \"D2S3\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0150-8f9879574c70:d01\", \"start\": 372, \"end\": 465, \"text\": \"Many of the label's releases are recorded at Gabriel's Real World Studios, at Box, Wiltshire.\"}, \"D2S4\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0150-8f9879574c70:d01\", \"start\": 466, \"end\": 521, \"text\": \"The label is distributed worldwide by Republic Records.\"}, \"D2S5\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0150-8f9879574c70:d01\", \"start\": 522, \"end\": 637, \"text\": \"There were previous distribution agreements with Caroline Records, Rykodisc, Virgin Records and Narada Productions.\"}, \"D2S6\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0150-8f9879574c70:d01\", \"start\": 638, \"end\": 640, \"text\": \"In\"}, \"D3S1\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0150-8f9879574c70:d02\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 256, \"text\": \"The Videos Big Blue Ball And I 'll Scratch Yours Real World Records Real World Studios Solid State Logic ( SSL ) Peter Gabriel discography Authority control databases : Geographic MusicBrainz place Retrieved from `` https : //en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php ?\"}, \"D3S2\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0150-8f9879574c70:d02\", \"start\": 257, \"end\": 704, \"text\": \"title=Real_World_Studios & oldid=1281828112 `` Categories : 1989 establishments in England Recording studios in England World music Multimedia Peter Gabriel Real World Records albums Box , Wiltshire Companies based in Wiltshire Hidden categories : Pages using gadget WikiMiniAtlas Articles with short description Short description is different from Wikidata Use dmy dates from April 2022 Coordinates on Wikidata Commons category link from Wikidata\"}, \"D4S1\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0150-8f9879574c70:d03\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 37, \"text\": \"Privacy | Cookies Website by Actually\"}}, \"original_cards\": [{\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0150-8f9879574c70:d00\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0150-8f9879574c70:d00:c0\", \"entity\": \"creator\", \"scope\": \"album\", \"claim\": \"Missy \\\"Misdemeanor\\\" Elliott is the creator of the album Real World.\", \"answer\": \"Missy \\\"Misdemeanor\\\" Elliott\", \"quote\": \"Da Real World Da Real World is the second studio album by American rapper Missy \\\"Misdemeanor\\\" Elliott, released on June 22, 1999 by EastWest Records America.\", \"original_document_number\": 1}, {\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0150-8f9879574c70:d01\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0150-8f9879574c70:d01:c0\", \"entity\": \"creator\", \"scope\": \"Real World\", \"claim\": \"Peter Gabriel is the creator of Real World.\", \"answer\": \"Peter Gabriel\", \"quote\": \"Real World Records Real World Records is a British record label started in 1989 by Peter Gabriel to record and produce world music, as well as his own releases.\", \"original_document_number\": 2}], \"R5_answers\": [\"Missy \\\"Misdemeanor\\\" Elliott\", \"Peter Gabriel\"], \"candidates\": [{\"id\": \"C0\", \"answer\": \"Missy \\\"Misdemeanor\\\" Elliott\", \"origin\": \"R5\"}, {\"id\": \"C1\", \"answer\": \"Peter Gabriel\", \"origin\": \"R5\"}]}"
